WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.410
Pumpkin carving at Halloween is a family tradition.
万圣节刻南瓜是我们家的传统。

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.470
We visit a local farm every October.
每年十月，我们都去当地一家农场。

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:13.800
In the pumpkin field, I compete with my three brothers and sister to seek out the biggest pumpkin.
在南瓜地里，我和三个弟弟、一个妹妹比赛，看谁能找出最大的南瓜。

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:23.170
My dad has a rule that we have to carry our pumpkins back home, and as the eldest child I have an advantage—I carried an 85-pounder back last year.
爸爸定了个规矩，南瓜得自己扛回家；我是家里的老大，占了优势——去年我就扛回了一个85磅重的大南瓜。

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:31.220
This year, it was hard to tell whether my prize or the one chosen by my 14-year-old brother, Jason, was the winner.
今年，很难说清是我选中的南瓜赢了，还是我14岁的弟弟杰森选的那个赢了。

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:38.180
Unfortunately we forgot to weigh them before taking out their insides, but I was determined to prove my point.
可惜我们忘了先称一称，就把瓜瓤掏了出来，可我还是下定决心要证明自己说得对。

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.620
All of us were hard at work at the kitchen table, with my mom filming the annual event.
我们全都围在厨房的桌子旁埋头忙活，妈妈在给这一年一度的活动录像。

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:51.530
I’m unsure now why I thought forcing my head inside the pumpkin would settle the matter, but it seemed to make perfect sense at the time.
现在我也说不清，当时为什么觉得把头硬塞进南瓜就能定输赢，可在那时，这似乎再合理不过了。

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:58.420
With the pumpkin resting on the table, hole uppermost, I bent over and pressed my head against the opening.
南瓜放在桌上，开口朝上，我弯下腰，把头抵在开口上。

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:07.380
At first I got jammed just above my eyes and then, as I went on with my task, unwilling to quit, my nose briefly prevented entry.
一开始，头卡在了眼睛上方；后来，我不肯罢休，接着往里挤，鼻子又一度让头进不去。

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.720
Finally I managed to put my whole head into it, like a cork forced into a bottle.
最后，我总算把整个脑袋塞了进去，就像软木塞硬塞进了瓶口。

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:17.230
I was able to straighten up with the huge pumpkin resting on my shoulders.
我直起身来，巨大的南瓜就架在了我的肩膀上。

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.670
My excitement was short-lived.
我的兴奋没持续多久。

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.690
The pumpkin was heavy.
南瓜很沉。

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:30.720
“I’m going to set it down, now,” I said, and with Jason helping to support its weight, I bent back over the table to give it somewhere to rest.
“我现在要把它放下来了。”我说。杰森帮忙托着南瓜的重量，我又俯身趴回桌上，好给它找个地方搁着。

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:38.000
It was only when I tried to remove my head that I realized getting out was going to be less straightforward than getting in.
直到想把头拔出来时，我才意识到，出来可没有进去那么容易。

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.450
When I pulled hard, my nose got in the way.
我一使劲拔，鼻子又挡住了。

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:49.720
I got into a panic as I pressed firmly against the table and moved my head around trying to find the right angle, but it was no use.
我慌了神，用力抵住桌子，转动脑袋想找到合适的角度，可一点用都没有。

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.580
“I can’t get it out!” I shouted, my voice sounding unnaturally loud in the enclosed space.
“我拔不出来了！”我大喊，在这封闭的空间里，我的声音听起来大得出奇。

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.170
It was five or six minutes though it felt much longer.
前后有五六分钟，可感觉要长得多。

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.640
The video was posted the Monday before Halloween.
视频在万圣节前的那个星期一发到了网上。
